      "status": "Acknowledged",
      "summary": "Roadway Sign Maintenance",
      "description": "Traffic light at Tuscarora High and Wild Plum Drive is a safety issue Any vehicles exiting the neighborhood immediately triggers light to change, causing drivers on Ballenger Creek Pike to accelerate to \"make the light\" before it turns red Drivers exiting the neighborhood (specifically right hand turns onto Ballenger Creek Pime) typically won't come to a complete stop before turning because they know they have already triggered the light cycle to change-so they roll right though the intersection, causing unsafe conditions to drivers and pedestrians This section of road is used by many school aged walkers, bicyclists and patrons of the Ballenger Creek Trail",
